# Cloudflare Pages custom headers — parsed by Pages, not served as an asset.
# Our static assets are NOT fingerprinted (stable names: /app.js, /landing.js,
# /offer.mjs, /showroom.css, /models/*/*.json, /quote.wasm, …), so a long browser
# cache serves STALE code after a deploy. Revalidate on every request instead:
# the browser still caches and sends a conditional request, getting a cheap 304
# when the file is unchanged (no re-download) and the new file immediately when it
# changed — so a deploy is picked up at once and stale content is never served.
# This is Cloudflare's recommended default for non-fingerprinted static sites.
# NB: _headers does NOT apply to Pages Functions (/api/*); those set their own
# short Cache-Control in functions/api/*.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
